<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alan I, King of Brittany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 907</span> · Also known as Alan the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alan I, called the Great, was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vannes">Vannes</a> and from about 890 king of Brittany. He led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bretons">Bretons</a> to a victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> at Questembert in 888 and reunited the country after a period of division. He was the last Breton ruler to bear the title of king; after his death the Vikings overran Brittany.</p></div>
